<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Calculus Derivatives & Integrals Reference Sheet - SmartLearn PDF</title>
  <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <link href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; background: #f8f9fa; color: #212529; padding: 40px; }
    .pdf-card { background: white; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); padding: 40px; max-width: 850px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .header-bar { border-bottom: 3px solid #0d6efd; padding-bottom: 15px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
    .formula-box { background: #e7f1ff; border-left: 4px solid #0d6efd; padding: 15px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 15px 0; font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    @media print {
      body { background: white; padding: 0; }
      .pdf-card { box-shadow: none; max-width: 100%; padding: 20px; }
      .no-print { display: none; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="pdf-card">
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center no-print mb-4">
      <a href="/notes.html" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to SmartLearn Library</a>
      <button onclick="window.print()" class="btn btn-primary fw-bold"><i class="fas fa-print"></i> Save / Print as PDF</button>
    </div>

    <div class="header-bar d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
      <div>
        <h2 class="fw-bold text-primary mb-1">🧮 Calculus Derivatives & Integrals Reference Sheet</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">SmartLearn Official Study Guide • Advanced Mathematics Series</p>
      </div>
      <span class="badge bg-primary fs-6 px-3 py-2">Mathematics</span>
    </div>

    <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mt-4">1. Fundamental Derivative Rules</h4>
    <div class="formula-box">
      • Power Rule: d/dx (xⁿ) = n·xⁿ⁻¹<br>
      • Product Rule: d/dx (u·v) = u'·v + u·v'<br>
      • Quotient Rule: d/dx (u/v) = (u'·v - u·v') / v²<br>
      • Chain Rule: d/dx [f(g(x))] = f'(g(x)) · g'(x)<br>
      • Exponential Rule: d/dx (eˣ) = eˣ<br>
      • Logarithmic Rule: d/dx (ln x) = 1/x
    </div>

    <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mt-4">2. Fundamental Integration Rules</h4>
    <div class="formula-box">
      • Power Rule: ∫ xⁿ dx = [xⁿ⁺¹ / (n + 1)] + C  (n ≠ -1)<br>
      • Log Rule: ∫ (1/x) dx = ln|x| + C<br>
      • Exponential: ∫ eˣ dx = eˣ + C<br>
      • Integration by Parts: ∫ u dv = u·v - ∫ v du
    </div>

    <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mt-4">3. Trigonometric Derivatives & Integrals</h4>
    <div class="formula-box">
      • d/dx (sin x) = cos x  |  ∫ cos x dx = sin x + C<br>
      • d/dx (cos x) = -sin x |  ∫ sin x dx = -cos x + C<br>
      • d/dx (tan x) = sec² x |  ∫ sec² x dx = tan x + C
    </div>

    <hr class="my-5">
    <div class="text-center text-muted small">
      <p>© 2026 SmartLearn Library — Verified Academic Study Resource 🎓</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
